The attached image (Fig. 3) illustrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is efficiently taken up by recruited immune cells. Panel A, a quantitative time-course, shows an early peak of neutrophils at 6 hours, followed by peaks of macrophages, antigen-presenting cells, and monocytes at Day 2, with inflammation substantially diminishing by Day 21. Panel B provides confocal microscopy images, demonstrating that fluorescently labeled Nano-11 (red) is internalized by various immune cells, including MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells and Mac-2+ macrophages, indicating that the nanoparticles are readily phagocytized at the injection site.